{
  "about": "Base-profile conformance (D29): panel value + client state -> visible rows. Every client flattens panels this way. `state` is {page?, filter?, open?: {row id: bool}}. A row is {id, depth, text, type, has_children, expanded, pinned, selectable}; `type` defaults to item, unknown types render as plain items. `missing` is what a client with `features` lacks from the panel's outer `requires`; an enhancement (list_detail) is used only when its own scoped `requires` has nothing missing. Generated by the Rust model (tests/client_conformance.rs, VQRO_FIXTURE_UPDATE=1) and reviewed; edit inputs, then regenerate. Element fallbacks (D29): a row with an unknown type or unmet scoped `requires` shows its `fallback` (row, rows or \"drop\"); without one it stays a plain item; fallback rows inherit the id (`<id>~<n>` for lists); chips likewise.",
  "base_features": [
    "items",
    "pages",
    "tree",
    "toolbar",
    "badges",
    "description",
    "menu",
    "input",
    "options",
    "select",
    "chips",
    "icon",
    "wrap"
  ],
